  "security_implications": "The chunk controls data flow to the KMAC engine for key manager operations (advance, identity, generate), handling byte masks, transaction beats, and error reporting. A fault containment gap (U1) allows dispatched transactions to continue even when cnt_err is asserted, risking corrupted data reaching KMAC and compromising key advance integrity or digest correctness. Additionally, cmd_chk being forced low during idle/clean states (U2) disables command cross-checking, potentially opening a window for unauthorized commands. The absence of explicit data wipe in StClean (U3) may leave key/digest residues.",
